From 09265b4b9da914636d1d3fa6722c54094914cdd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yokunade
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:44:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sources): add mysql_cdc source and a shared CDC core

Adds a `mysql_cdc` source that captures row-level changes from MySQL 8.0+
through the binlog, and a change-data-capture core (`src/sources/cdc/`)
that future connectors can share:

- snapshots: incremental (chunked reads while streaming, DBLog watermarks;
  needs GTIDs) or blocking (consistent, optionally parallel); snapshots of
  newly captured tables (`snapshot_new_tables`); re-snapshot when the
  binlog was purged (`snapshot_mode: when_needed`)
- row-based binlog streaming, resume by GTID set or file/position,
  reconnects and heartbeats
- event formats: `record` (metadata + row, or with `record_images:
  before_and_after` a `record` holding `before` and `after`, where a
  delete's `after` is the row's key, `pk_override` included) or Debezium
  envelopes, with Debezium value representations (decimal, binary, JSON,
  time precision)
- `seq`: one fixed-width, text-sortable sequence per source; replayed
  events keep their `seq`
- outputs: row changes; `control` (`schema_change`, `truncate`,
  `snapshot_completed`); `table_schemas` (one schema document per table
  definition); `offsets` (published commit points); `observe`
  (unacknowledged copies of every event, for viewers such as a live feed)
- offsets at transaction boundaries, stored atomically and only after
  end-to-end acknowledgement (at-least-once)
- `single_writer_lock`: an Azure blob lease, so only one instance captures
  a server at a time
- `offset_recovery`: a source whose stored offset is lost resumes from
  the last published offset, which now carries the whole stored offset
  (`checkpoint`); it starts from scratch only into an empty folder
- `unplanned_snapshots: hold` (default): a re-snapshot after a purged
  binlog waits for approval (`resnapshot_approved`), and tables whose
  snapshot state was lost are streamed but held (`held_tables`, a
  `snapshot_held` control event) until an operator releases them
- database/table/column include and exclude lists, `pk_override`, online
  schema-change shadow tables skipped
- `azure_blob` sink: `blob_extension` and `blob_overwrite` options
- Cargo.lock: pins `mysql_async` 0.37.1, `mysql_common` 0.37.3 and their
  dependencies, so builds are reproducible
- Cargo.lock: rustls-webpki 0.103.15 -> 0.103.16 (RUSTSEC-2026-0382)
- contrib/mysql_cdc: documentation, Docker test environment (MySQL 8.4.13,
  Azurite 3.37.0, Azure CLI 2.91.0, pinned by digest), end-to-end, load,
  readiness and snapshot benchmark scripts, example configs
